{# ONE CARD GRAMMAR for every preset, whoever wrote it: the name, the whole
   trade-off line, and a quiet meta row with the widget count and the one action.

   THE CARD IS A HANDLE, NOT A PICTURE. Seeing what a preset looks like is the
   canvas's job, one click away; a thumbnail of a grid earns nothing and most
   people never read it as a page.

   EVERY CARD IS THE SAME OBJECT IN EVERY STATE. Selecting one changes its
   border, its tint and its badge — never its geometry, and never what it holds.
   Anything a state needs to ADD (a name field, an Apply button) belongs to the
   toolbar below the strips: growing a card would reflow the whole strip under
   the cursor that just clicked it.

   Parameters: kind ('design'|'mine'|'new'), preset (WidgetPreset|null), active,
   and — for the 'new' card, which has no preset behind it — label, description,
   layout, extraClass. Clicking a card that is not active PREVIEWS it, which is
   client-side and needs no route; assets/widgets.js reads data-preset-kind and
   data-preset-id. #}

{% set label = preset is not null ? preset.label : (label|default('')) %}
{% set description = preset is not null ? preset.description : (description|default('')) %}
{% set layout = preset is not null ? preset.layout : (layout|default({})) %}
{% set count = layout|length %}

<div class="w-preset{{ active ? ' w-preset-active' }}{{ extraClass|default('') }}"
     data-preset-kind="{{ kind }}" data-preset-id="{{ preset is not null ? preset.id : '' }}"
     role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="{{ active ? 'true' : 'false' }}">
    <div class="w-presettop">
        <span class="w-presetname">{{ label }}</span>
        {% if active %}
            <span class="w-presetflag w-presetflag-active">{{ ux_icon('lucide:check') }}Active</span>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
    {# The whole line, wrapped — a trade-off cut off mid-sentence is worse than no
       trade-off. The grid row equalises the cards' heights. #}
    <p class="w-presetsub">{{ description }}</p>
    <div class="w-presetmeta">
        <span class="w-presetcount">{{ count }} widget{{ count == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span>
        <span class="w-presetgo">{{ active ? 'On your dashboard' : 'Preview' }}{{ ux_icon('lucide:arrow-right') }}</span>
    </div>
</div>
